To find the area of a polygon given its vertices, one of the methods is the shoelace formula. The formula is as follows:

$$
\text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} | \sum_{i=1}^{n} (x_i y_{i+1} - x_{i+1} y_i) |
$$

where $ (x_{n+1}, y_{n+1}) = (x_1, y_1) $.

